1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
The record says: delivered on time, in full. What actually happened: one pallet line held the wrong pack size.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:09,300
Monday 22 June, 6:12 am. The warehouse truck reaches Store 014 inside its slot, read the way a data team reads it.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:15,200
The OTIF dashboard: 88% for June. The 22 June delivery counts as perfect.

4
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:21,600
All 10 data tests pass: every record was written from the same pick. The pallets were never weighed.

5
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:28,000
Four stock corrections in two buildings net to ₹80. Nothing to chase.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,400
Paired, they are equal and opposite, 16 cases each way. The trace names SHP-260622, line 1: 160 packs of 1 kg.

7
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:42,300
An AI assistant with a domain layer: 7 of 7 answers right, not 1. On time, but not in full.

8
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,700
OTIF reconciled with the counts: 84%, what the shelf got. The 5 kg shelf stood empty 51.5 open hours.

9
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:55,100
Weigh every pallet: caught at dispatch. The shelf stays full, and OTIF falls to 84%.

10
00:00:55,100 --> 00:01:00,100
Every record agreed. That is exactly why nobody checked the pallet.
